{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JThND3978CxdMmGn9mMWNW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":4}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d69aaa1f-56b4-4f39-a0fb-c646169c1f0d","uuid":"154f2b1f-937c-469e-aa41-4ea022c27db2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:59:53.868Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":4}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JThND3978CxdMmGn9mMWNW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
